\f1\fs22 Tony had spent three hours orchestrating the perfect evening. The view from his penthouse was set to "Golden Hour Aurora Australis\'94. Even nature couldn't compete with his wealth anymore. The fourteen-course meal prepared by his personal Elvi chef sat under warming domes, each dish more obscenely expensive than the last.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"So," he said, spreading his arms wide as Sarah entered, "what do you think? King of the world, baby."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah took in the absurd luxury with a mixture of amusement and unease, but her eyes kept returning to Tony himself. He looked... extraordinary. His skin had an almost luminescent quality, his eyes bright and clear, his entire bearing radiating vitality. When had he become so devastatingly handsome?\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"It's certainly... shiny."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Shiny? This is the apex of civilization!" Tony gestured grandly. "Voice-activated climate control, a bidet that plays \'91Evolve Me Tender.' I've got it all."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Fisher glided forward, offering Sarah a drink. "Champagne from the Napoleon cellar, madam? It predates even the Dark Ages."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Just water, thanks." Sarah watched as Tony commanded various appliances with theatrical hand gestures, each device responding with unnecessary fanfare. The grace in his movements, the effortless charm\'97when had he developed such confident magnetism? "Since when do you have servants?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"They're staff," Tony corrected. "And they love working here. Right, Fisher?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Indeed, sir. Though I must note that yesterday you referred to us as 'Brylcreem security,'" Fisher replied with artificial cheerfulness.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"That was before I adjusted to my new station in life." Tony guided Sarah to the dining area where he'd arranged their seats at opposite ends of a twenty-foot table. "You know what else changed? Me. I'm ready now, Sarah. Ready for... us."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The absurdity of the setup\'97shouting across a crystal-laden table to have an intimate conversation\'97actually made Sarah laugh. Tony, encouraged, began detailing his newfound sophistication between courses of increasingly ridiculous dishes.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"And check this out," he said, standing up to demonstrate the apartment's voice controls. "Tony wants music. Sexy music."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Immediately, an orchestra of Elvis's most romantic ballads swelled through hidden speakers.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Tony wants mood lighting."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The lights dimmed to a golden glow, somehow making his hair gleam despite its recent lack of grooming, enhancing the almost preternatural wellness that radiated from him.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Tony wants\'97"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Tony wants to stop talking in third person?" Sarah suggested, but she was smiling now, drawn to this vibrant version of Tony despite her conflicted feelings.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>As the evening progressed, Tony's boyish enthusiasm mixed with his new confidence created an unexpectedly appealing combination. He made self-deprecating jokes about his wealth while still basking in it, a perfect balance that drew Sarah in despite her better judgment. She couldn't stop noticing how his skin seemed to glow with health, how his movements had gained an almost athletic fluidity.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"You know," she said later, as they moved to the vast living room, "I think I preferred you as Mr. Fairy Boxers."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony's grin was pure delight. "You remember those?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Hard to forget. You were so proud of them, even when you were sleeping in refrigerators."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Now I could buy a thousand pairs. Want to see my collection?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Please tell me you didn't actually\'97"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Framed. In the master suite. Very tasteful."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>This made her laugh again, and suddenly they were closer than they'd been in months. Tony caught her hand, his skin warm and vibrant against hers, thumb tracing her knuckles as the mood shifted.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Sarah..." he began, but she was already leaning toward him.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The kiss started tentatively but deepened as months of separation dissolved. When Tony's hand moved to her waist, she didn't pull away. Instead, she let herself be drawn into his orbit once more, remembering why she'd fallen for him despite all logic. His touch sent shivers through her\'97not just from desire, but from something else. A recognition. A knowing.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"We shouldn't," she murmured against his lips.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Probably not," he agreed, continuing the kiss.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>They moved to the plush sofa, Tony's confidence making the transition smooth. His hands were sure as they began removing her jacket, his touch familiar yet new with his newfound assurance. Sarah responded, matching his intensity as they shed both clothing and inhibitions, even as a voice in her head screamed warnings about what she might have already done.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>But as Tony led her toward the master suite, past walls adorned with priceless art and custom displays, something shifted in Sarah's stomach. Not the queasiness of early pregnancy, but something deeper\'97a revulsion that seemed to emanate from the very walls.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Sarah?" Tony noticed her hesitation at the threshold of his bedroom.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"I..." She pressed her palm against the doorframe, her skin crawling. "You have no idea what that man did to me."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"What man? Shakti? If this is about the wedding\'97"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Jamison Hardy!" The name burst from her lips like a confession. "That monster, he... I can't..." She swayed slightly, gripping the wall for support.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Sarah, Hardy died like a hundred years ago. What are you talking about?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Horror dawned in her eyes as she realized what she'd said. She struggled to recover, her voice shaking. "I live in his shadow every day, and now, so do you. This place, this wealth\'97it's all built on his money, his legacy, his crimes."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony reached for her, concerned. "Baby, you're not making sense. Come here, let me\'97"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>But his touch now felt wrong, tainted by the wealth that surrounded them and by what she feared he'd become because of her. Where moments ago his confidence and vitality had been attractive, now they felt dangerous. The casual way he wore this new skin made her stomach churn.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"I changed my mind," she said abruptly, rebuttoning her blouse with shaking fingers. "This was a mistake. The pregnancy\'97I'm feeling sick. I need to leave."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Sarah, wait. What just happened?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"I can't explain it," she said, backing away from him. "I just... I can't be here. I'm sorry."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony's expression darkened with hurt, then defensive anger. "Fine. You know what? Go back to your husband, your perfect little family. I'll just call up a dozen Elvinas to spend the night with me."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"You'll what?" Sarah's voice was sharp with alarm.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"You heard me," Tony said, grabbing his communication device. "I've got numbers for days."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"You'll sleep with them?" Her tone was somewhere between question and accusation.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony chuckled, misunderstanding her concern. "Well, not all of them, of course. I'm not that virile." He paused, smirking. "Though something strange happens when they sleep with me. They all look younger afterward. More attractive. I'm good for their health, Sarah."\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah stared at him, her face draining of color. "You're a monster," she whispered.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"What? I thought you'd approve of sharing the wealth!" Tony spread his arms, missing her horror entirely. "I'm helping people! Look at me\'97never felt better. Might live forever at this rate!"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"Stop!" Sarah covered her ears, backing toward the door. "You don't understand what you're\'97"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>"What? Making people happy? Giving them the time of their lives?"\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>With a choked sob, Sarah fled his penthouse, leaving Tony standing alone in his perfectly curated paradise, wondering how he'd managed to lose her again despite having everything money could buy\'97and apparently, the secret to eternal youth.\

